B.Rr=new A.eS("humanoid","Humanoid","The default humanoid shape.","All checks to heal or shield you have a +1 to success.","The first time each situation a character fails a Convince check, they may reroll the check.",B.d7,B.jp)
B.QJ=new A.e_("Meetups","{Half Level}",!0)
B.akq=s([B.QJ],t.G)
B.R7=new A.fl("quadrupedal_herding","Herding","You may not climb. You have difficult prone. Gain +1 Speed.\nTrampling: [Reaction] During your turn, spend your reaction; you may move through an enemy who is a smaller size than you. Make a Status Check vs Str. On Success, deal {Difference in size between the target and you d6}.\nHerd: [Reaction] During a target ally's turn, spend your reaction and move up to the target's speed as long as you end within 6 spaces of the target.","{Half Level} times per story, you summon a bunch of casual friends who are all meeting up with you. You must explain the reason for the meetup at this place and time.",B.akq)
B.QB=new A.e_("Silent Kills","{Half Level}",!0)
B.anX=s([B.QB],t.G)
B.R6=new A.fl("quadrupedal_pouncing","Pouncing","[Reaction] At the start of an enemy turn, spend your reaction, dash {Half Level} to a free space range 1 of an enemy, and make an Attack vs Str. On success, grapple the target and give them {Half Level d6} Bleed.","{Half Level} times per story, when you attack from concealment with a melee blow and kill your prey, you don't break concealment.",B.anX)
B.QI=new A.e_("Dodges","{Half Level}",!0)
B.aic=s([B.QI],t.G)
B.Rf=new A.fl("quadrupedal_springing","Springing","Ignore difficult terrain. You may not climb, and have difficult prone. [Reaction] Start of any turn, spend your reaction and dash {Half Level} spaces. You may target another creature; if you do, make a status check vs Str. On success, knock them prone, then dash {Half Level} spaces to a free space. Otherwise dash to a free space adjacent to the target. Allies may make a Dex defense to resist falling prone.","{Half Level} times per story, when you would be grabbed, grappled, or restrained, instead dodge out of the way.",B.aic)
B.akO=s([B.R7,B.R6,B.Rf],t.CT)
B.Rq=new A.eS("Quadrupedal","Quadrupedal","Difficult Prone: To stand from prone, you must make and succeed on either a Brute or Finesse check, and it also requires the use of all your speed. If an effect would reduce the cost to stand from prone, instead it costs Half Speed to stand.","","",B.d7,B.akO)
B.QK=new A.e_("Hideaways","{Level}",!0)
B.aib=s([B.QK],t.G)
B.Ri=new A.eS("bodyplan_hexapodal","Hexapodal","","Ignore Difficult Terrain. You have +1 to grapple checks. When enemies force you to move, you move half as far. You may not be knocked prone; when you would gain prone, instead lose {Vitality} health. You may not reduce or resist this damage.\nScuttle: [Reaction] Start of any turn, spend your reaction and dash {Level} to a free space.","{Level} times per story, after succeeding a defense, you scuttle under something or out of sight of whatever caused you to defend. Then make a conceal check to hide from it.",B.aib,B.jp)
B.QG=new A.e_("Whispers","{Level}",!0)
B.alf=s([B.QG],t.G)
B.Rm=new A.eS("bodyplan_serpent","Serpent","","Ignore difficult terrain and reduce your speed by 2. It costs only 1 speed to stand from prone. Climbing and swimming do not cost extra speed. You may move through other creatures' spaces and your movement doesn't provoke attacks. Before making an attack, you may dash 1 space toward your target.","{Level} times per story, while concealed, you can whisper to a person you can see and only they can hear you.",B.alf,B.jp)
B.QQ=new A.e_("Lures","{Half Level}",!0)
B.ama=s([B.QQ],t.G)
B.Rj=new A.eS("bodyplan_mermaid","Mermaid","","Reduce your speed by 2. Moving through water doesn't cost extra movement. Gain {3 * Vitality} bonus Health and +1/+2 range on Attacks.","{Half Level} times per story, lure all characters that can hear you to your location. Your voice will only lure them for a short time, or till they are harmed.",B.ama,B.jp)
B.QA=new A.e_("Flights","{Half Level}",!0)
B.anY=s([B.QA],t.G)
B.Rk=new A.eS("bodyplan_winged","Flying","","You have -1 speed when not flying. You may start any situation already concentrating on natural flight.\n\nNatural Flight: [Reaction] During your Turn, spend your reaction and begin concentrating on natural flight. While concentrating, you gain 1 bonus speed, you dash instead of moving, and may fly vertically while moving. You must be in a free space on the ground to use abilities, weapon attacks, or at the end of your turn. You may concentrate on this in addition to other effects. Make only 1 concentration check for all the effects.\n\nIf you are knocked prone, your flight ends. Standing from prone still requires movement, and you may not fly until you are standing.","{Half Level} times per story, you can fly out of any scene or fly into any scene containing a party member. If anyone asks how you got there you must explain.",B.anY,B.jp)
B.QL=new A.e_("Bounces","{Level}",!0)
B.ao4=s([B.QL],t.G)
B.Rp=new A.eS("bodyplan_bouncing","Bouncing","","Your movement is inconsistent and difficult to predict. Your movement doesn't provoke attacks and you may move through other creatures' spaces. At the end of your turn, choose a random direction and dash {1d6 /2} spaces in that direction. This counts as forced movement for colliding with terrain or being thrown into a pit.","{Level} times per story, after succeeding a Str, Dex, or Vit defense, you begin to bounce chaotically, preventing anyone from grabbing hold of you for a minute.",B.ao4,B.jp)
B.QN=new A.e_("Squeezes","{Level}",!0)
B.amQ=s([B.QN],t.G)
B.R5=new A.fl("swarm_damage","Biting Swarm","At the end of your turn, deal {Half Level d6} damage to enemies in your spaces.","",B.d7)
B.R9=new A.fl("swarm_heal","Mending Swarm","At the end of your turn, heal allies in your spaces {Half Level d6}.","",B.d7)
B.R8=new A.fl("swarm_shield","Sheltering Swarm","At the end of your turn, give allies in your spaces {Half Level d6} shield.","",B.d7)
B.aiU=s([B.R5,B.R9,B.R8],t.CT)
B.Ro=new A.eS("bodyplan_swarm","Swarm","","Increase your size by 1. You cannot be flanked and don't benefit from flanking. You automatically succeed checks to escape grapple. Creatures may occupy your spaces and your spaces count as free spaces for abilities. You may move through enemies' spaces, and enemies may move through you.\nIf two or more swarms overlap, at the end of any creature's turn who is inside of the overlap, including the swarms, they must succeed a Str defense or take {Level d6} Bludgeoning damage.","{Level} times per story, you can squeeze through a door, window, through any seal or any gap.",B.amQ,B.aiU)
B.QF=new A.e_("Wall Bursts","{Level /3}",!0)
B.apk=s([B.QF],t.G)
B.R4=new A.fl("vehicle_armored_transport","Armored Transport","You resist damage caused by attacks targeting allies riding you. [Reaction] After an ally becomes adjacent to you, you may spend your reaction to have them start riding you, and move into your space wherever you choose.","{Level /3} times per story, you may suddenly enter the scene by bursting through a wall.",B.apk)
B.QO=new A.e_("Burnouts","{Half Level}",!0)
B.amx=s([B.QO],t.G)
B.Rh=new A.fl("vehicle_race_tires","Race Tires","Gain +2 speed.","{Half Level} times per story, you may flee the scene at high speed. People may give chase but you still burn rubber out.",B.amx)
B.QS=new A.e_("Overruns","{Half Level}",!0)
B.ai3=s([B.QS],t.G)
B.Rc=new A.fl("vehicle_treads","Treads","Ignore difficult terrain. You resist damage from collision regardless of success.","{Half Level} times per story, you may go up and over anything. If it cannot support your weight it is crushed underneath you without damaging you.",B.ai3)
B.QV=new A.e_("Pulls","{Half Level}",!0)
B.aml=s([B.QV],t.G)
B.Rb=new A.fl("vehicle_winch","Winch","Winch: [Reaction] During an ally's turn, move up to {Level} in a line without provoking attacks. You may do this when prone, but you take {Half Vitality d6} damage.\nHook: [Reaction] During an ally's turn, make a Melee Attack vs Dex targeting one enemy range {1 + Half Level}. On success, deal {Half Level d6} damage and pull the target up to {Half Level + 1} spaces. You may target allies but they take only {1d6} damage.","{Half Level} times per story, you may pull anyone you see to you.",B.aml)
B.Rd=new A.fl("vehicle_forklift","Forklift","When you succeed on an attack against an adjacent enemy, you may lift the target until the start of your next turn. While lifted, the target is restrained, doesn't provoke attacks, and remains adjacent whenever you move, dash, or teleport.","",B.d7)
B.Rg=new A.fl("vehicle_flying","Flying","Same as the Flying body plan: you have -1 speed when not flying and may use Natural Flight.","",B.d7)
B.amK=s([B.R4,B.Rh,B.Rc,B.Rb,B.Rd,B.Rg],t.CT)
B.Rl=new A.eS("bodyplan_vehicle","Vehicle","","Gain +2 speed. You cannot climb. Forced movement targeting you is halved but damage from being forced into terrain is tripled.\nProne: When you are knocked prone, you cannot move nor dash, nor can you end the prone effect. Adjacent allies may spend a [Reaction] or [Action] to remove your prone.\nRiding: Adjacent allies may ride you, as long as at least 1 of their spaces can fit in your space, and that space doesn't contain another ally. For every space worth of ally unable to fit, reduce your speed by 1. While riding, players are prone, they may still be targeted for attacks, and they resist all damage and you take an equal amount of damage as they do if you were not also targeted by the attack. To begin riding and to stop riding players must pay the cost to stand from prone. Hexapod allies aren't damaged for becoming prone because of riding, and stop riding by spending 1 movement point.\nCollision: [Reaction] During your turn, you may move through an enemy who is a smaller size than you. Make a Status Check vs Str. On Success, deal {Vitality d12} Bludgeoning damage to you and the target and the target is knocked prone. On Problems, you take {Vitality d6} damage or are knocked prone.","",B.d7,B.amK)
B.Re=new A.fl("parts_universal","Universal"," Any of your allies may be your host, you can use a [Action] to move from your current host to a target ally. When an ally moves within {Half Level} spaces of you, you may spend your [Reaction] to move from your current host to that ally.","",B.d7)
B.Ra=new A.fl("parts_specific","Specific","You can only have a specific character be your host. At the end of your turn and your host turn, you and your host may give each other Shield and Health. During your turn, you may force your host to move up to {Half your speed}, this movement does provoke attacks. Whenever you or your host heals or gains shields you may give some or all of it to the other.","",B.d7)
B.ajA=s([B.Re,B.Ra],t.CT)
B.Rn=new A.eS("bodyplan_parts","Parts","Your body is a part of another character\u2019s body. You are connected to your host and cannot be separated from each other. Effects that move, dash, teleport, slow, or restrain your host also apply to you and vise versa.You may not use movement points. When you take the [run] action, you may force your host to move up to your speed and this movement can provoke attacks. When you take the [Retreat] action, you may force your host to move half your speed without provoking attacks. When your host doesn\u2019t provoke attacks of opportunity, you also avoid attacks of opportunity. For each size you are more than your host, reduce their speed by 1. If you are smaller or larger than your host, you may reposition yourself relative to your host during your turn so that you are within at least 1 of their spaces. When you die, you must run a generic body with no combat features from spawn to a space adjacent to your host to respond in your body. When your host dies, you are stuck attached to their body until your host moves to space adjacent to you and uses an object interaction to pick you up. When you pick this, choose between being Universal, or Specific.","","",B.d7,B.ajA)
B.cp=s([B.Rr,B.Rq,B.Ri,B.Rm,B.Rj,B.Rk,B.Rp,B.Ro,B.Rl,B.Rn],A.aq("A<eS>"))
B.NV=new A.q2(0,"static")
B.aC6=new A.dm("source_innate","Innate","The character can use the ability as much as they like, using a Source value of {Half Power}. If the feature only has the innate source gain +1 to the source value.","If you only have innate as your only source, gain +1 to skill results.","Next scene gain +1 to skills you're proficient in, or next situation start with {Power + Level} shield.","You have -1 to attacks and proficient skills.","{Half Power}",B.NV,"epic_source_innate",!1,null,null,B.a8,B.a8,null)
B.NX=new A.q2(5,"minion")
B.aCH=new A.c1("Pawns","Instead of a normal chump, you have {Their Vitality} Pawns with 1 HP each. Whenever they gain shield they gain 1 shield, blocking 1 attack. If they have spectral or gain Resistance to all, they instead have 2 HP.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCE=new A.c1("Melee","HP {4 * Level * Their Vitality}. [Minion] Make a Melee Attack vs Str targeting 1 enemy range 1. On Success, deal {Half points d8} damage.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCm=new A.c1("Range","HP {3 * Level * Their Vitality}. [Minion] Make a Ranged Attack vs Dex targeting 1 enemy range 6/12. On Success, deal {Half points d6} damage.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCk=new A.c1("Repair","HP {2 * Level * Their Vitality}. Repair [Minion] Make a status check targeting an adjacent Ally. On Success: Heal {Half points d8}.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCS=new A.c1("Shielding","HP {2 * Level * Their Vitality}. Shield [Minion] Make a status check targeting a range 1 ally. On success, they gain {Half points d6} shield.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCD=new A.c1("Familiar","HP {3 * Level * Their Vitality}. [Minion] You may target your abilities and skills from your minion's space. When you do, gain a +1 to the result of attacks, skills or status checks.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCX=new A.c1("Creation","HP {3 * Level * Their Vitality}. [Minion] Trigger a combat feature action with a source of {points / 4}. Choose the combat feature when you choose those.",B.a8,!1)
B.ajN=s([B.aCH,B.aCE,B.aCm,B.aCk,B.aCS,B.aCD,B.aCX],t.AJ)
B.aBW=new A.dm("source_companion","Companion","Your Companion is another character who takes their turn at the same time as you. When you trigger abilities of this source, your companion performs the ability using their stats with a source value of {Half Level}. If you do not trigger an ability of this source using your [Action] on your turn, your companion may trigger their [Minion] ability. You may have multiple companions with dm approval, treating each as a separate source.\nWhen you gain a companion, build a chump of your level but without a chump action, or combat features. Your companion has a Body Composition and Body Size but doesn't gain any bonuses related to the Body Composition or Body Size. Pick one of the below companion options, which changes the companion's Max HP.\nCompanions do not have turns but act during your turn. Companions are characters for the purposes of effects. Companions have reactions, and can concentrate. They may move up to their speed on each of your turns. If you perform a [Run] or [Retreat] your companions also take the action.","When you fail a skill or defense check, you may have your companion make the check instead. You may do this {points} times per Story.","Your companion starts next situation with {Level * Their Vitality} Shield.","Your companion has a -1 to check results.","{Half Level}",B.NX,"epic_source_companion",!1,null,null,B.ajN,B.a8,"{1}")
B.w6=new A.q2(7,"inventory")
B.aCu=new A.c1("Huckable","Increase range of abilities by {Level/3}",B.a8,!1)
B.aCb=new A.c1("Dangerous","Target all characters range 1 of any of the targets and deal {Level/3 d6} damage to them.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCz=new A.c1("Dampening","Target all enemies range {Level/3} of any of the targets and reduce their shields by {Level/3 d6}.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCa=new A.c1("Energizing","Target all Allies range {Level/3} of any of the targets and they gain {Level/3} speed until the end of their next turn.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCi=new A.c1("Empowering","Allies targeted by the ability deal {Level/3} d6 extra damage on their first attack they succeed on each turn.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCv=new A.c1("Protective","Target all allies range {Level/3} of any of the targets and give them {Level/3 d6} shields.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCL=new A.c1("Regenerative","Target all allies range 1 of any of the targets and heal them {Level/3 d10}.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCt=new A.c1("Unstable","Before using the ability make a create check, on success gain a source mod of 1, on failure lose health equal to your create level.",B.a8,!1)
B.al8=s([B.aCu,B.aCb,B.aCz,B.aCa,B.aCi,B.aCv,B.aCL,B.aCt],t.AJ)
B.aC3=new A.dm("source_craft","Craft","The character gains their powers from consumable creations that they make during combat. At the start of your turn, make a create check, on success gain 1 ingredient. When using an ability, the character must spend 1 ingredient, gaining its effects and a source of {Power}. For every 4 points of this source, the character gains 1 ingredient type from below, minimum 1. Whenever you spend an ingredient, the ingredient's type effect is added to the ability's effect. If the ability requires success, the effect only occurs if you succeed. You start each encounter with 1 ingredient of each type you know. You may create with 1 free hand. You cannot concentrate on the abilities of this source. When an ability would call for concentration, instead make a status check on the start of each of the target\u2019s turns, on failure the effect ends for the target.\n[Action] gain {Half Power} ingredients of your choice.\n[Reaction] When you fail a status effect check against a target within range 6, spend your reaction and an ingredient to cause the check to succeed instead.","After you succeed on a skill check, gain 1 craft and pick a skill check. You and your allies can use the craft to gain advantage on that type of check. You may do this up to {points} times each Story. You do not gain crafts for a check in which you used a craft.","Start the next situation with 2 ingredients of each type you know and have a +1 to create checks to create ingredients.","You start the next situation with no starting ingredients and have a -1 to create checks to create ingredients.","{Power}",B.w6,"epic_source_craft",!1,null,null,B.al8,B.a8,"{points / 4}")
B.w5=new A.q2(6,"transformation")
B.aCh=new A.c1("Melee","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, target an enemy range 1 and deal {points /2 d12} Damage.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCR=new A.c1("Ranged","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, target an enemy range 4 and deal {points /2 d10} Damage.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCp=new A.c1("Elusive","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, Your movement doesn\u2019t provoke attacks and you gain {points /2} Speed until the end of your turn.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCf=new A.c1("Barrier","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, Gain {points /2 d10} Shield and until the start of your next turn, allies range 2 may spend your shield when taking damage. On Problems, allies range 2 may spend your shield when taking damage until the start of your next turn.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCO=new A.c1("Regenerative","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, Heal {points /2 d6}.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCq=new A.c1("Armored","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, Gain a +1 to defense results and resistance to {points /3} defenses until the start of your next turn. When you pick this, pick the defenses. On Problems, you gain only the resistances.",B.a8,!1)
B.ajl=s([B.aCh,B.aCR,B.aCp,B.aCf,B.aCO,B.aCq],t.AJ)
B.aC2=new A.dm("source_form","Form","The character gains their power through altering their form. Once per situation, you transform into your alternate form before you activate one of your form source powers and remain changed as long as you are concentrating. You may only use this source when concentrating on your form, using a source value of {Power}. While in a form, you may concentrate on up to {Power} additional effects. When you lose concentration on your form, you lose concentration on these additional effects.\nWhen you choose this, pick a new body size, composition and defense class which replace your character's while in the form. When you pick your form, pick one of the below effects.\nYou may have multiple different forms, each different form is considered a separate source, Having its own usage and only being activatable when in the corresponding form. You may be concentrating on multiple forms at the same time, at the start of your turn select one of your forms to use its size, composition and defense class until your next turn. When concentrating on multiple forms, you may use any of those forms abilities regardless of which forms size you select. When concentrating on multiple forms, your extra forms do not grant you the ability to concentrate on extra effects per form.","When you pick this, choose different skill proficiencies for your form. You enter your form for the rest of the scene {Half points} times per Story, gaining one of the below effects.\nTerrifying: When you Succeed on an attack, or succeed a check to harm or destroy things, cause nearby civilians to flee in terror.\nLurking: If you haven't been seen in your form, you have advantage on conceal checks. Otherwise you gain +1 to conceal.\nAlluring: You have a +1 to convince results.","Next situation, you have advantage on concentrating on your form.","Next situation, you have disadvantage on concentrating on your form.","{Power}",B.w5,"epic_source_form",!1,null,null,B.ajl,B.a8,"{1}")
B.aC4=new A.dm("source_gadgets","Gadgets","The character gains their powers from created objects. Every combat feature is a unique object or a part in another unique object, that can appear as anything but has the properties of a single Implement selected when you take the feature. When you use the gadget, you have a source value of {Power + 1}. You may use the gadget once, then you must fix the gadget to use it again. If multiple features are in the same object, each feature can be used and fixed independently.\nFix: [Action] fix all of your Gadgets.\nJerryRig: [Reaction] During your or allies turn, you may spend your reaction and fix 1 gadget.","For each of your gadgets, You may gain advantage or +1 on results on a skill check. You may not do this again with this gadget until you either make a skill check with disadvantage or -1 to results.","Choose 1 of your gadgets and the first time you activate it in the next situation, you don't need to fix it.","Randomly choose 1 of your gadgets; it starts the next situation requiring a fix before you can use it.","{Power + 1}",B.w6,"epic_source_gadgets",!1,null,null,B.a8,B.a8,null)
B.aC5=new A.dm("source_granted_power","Granted Power","The character gets their features from a powerful entity. They may use their powers {2 * points} times per story. They regain all uses after each story. Your source value is {Power + 1}. Abilities of this source require the use of an implement.","You have {2 * points} blessings per Story. When you fail a skill check, you may pay 1 blessing to reroll. At the end of a situation or combat encounter, regain all your blessings.","Regain {points / 2} granted power usages.","Whenever you use a granted power usage, make a Vit defense; on problems suffer {vitality d6} damage.","{Power + 1}",B.NV,"epic_source_granted_power",!0,null,null,B.a8,B.a8,null)
B.w4=new A.q2(3,"heat")
B.aCQ=new A.c1("Shield","Target you and allies range {Power}, and Gain {half points d6} shield.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCY=new A.c1("Burning","Target Enemies range {Power} and give them {half points d6} Burn. Pick the damage type and target when you pick this.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCd=new A.c1("Growing","Each time you overload, increase the damage done by all attacks of this overload by 1d6, to a max bonus of {Power + points /3 d6}.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCZ=new A.c1("Warp","Target you and allies range {Power} and teleport each target to a free space within {Half points +1}.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCA=new A.c1("Combat Feature","Select a Combat Feature and trigger that as an overload effect using a source value of {Half Power + Half points}.",B.a8,!0)
B.alQ=s([B.aCQ,B.aCY,B.aCd,B.aCZ,B.aCA],t.AJ)
B.aBX=new A.dm("source_heat","Heat","The character gains their power through a slowly growing process, like a steam engine, or channeling spirit, or eating a big sandwich. Whenever you use an ability of this source, you gain 1 heat up to {Power + 1} and then do the ability using your heat as the source. When you would gain a heat but are at the max, instead you gain an overheat effect, and after you perform the ability, set your heat to 0. You pick the overheat effect when you pick the feature. Each overheat effect is a separate source. Features of the same overheat effect share heat, and you track each overheat effects heat levels separately.","During a situation, before making a roll you may warm up making the check with a -1 to the results. After warming up, for the rest of the situation you make that skill check with a +1 to results.","Start the next situation at {Half Power} heat.","The first time you would overheat in the next situation, instead set your heat to {Half Power}.","{1}",B.w4,"epic_source_heat",!1,null,"{Power + 1}",B.alQ,B.a8,null)
B.w3=new A.q2(1,"resource")
B.aC_=new A.dm("source_intuitive_magic","Intuitive Magic","The caster can freely cast their magic. You require an implement to use this source. They have {2 * Power * points} Max MP that they regain at the start of each Story. When they use a feature they must spend at least 1 MP and may spend up to {Power + 1} MP using a feature as the Source Value. On problems with an attack or status check, you pay only 1 MP.\nOvercasting: You may push the limits of your magic and spend {Power + Half Power} MP. When you do, if you get problems, you lose {Vitality d6} health which can't be shielded or resisted.","You may spend 2 MP to gain advantage on a skill or defense check. If multiple allies are making the same check, you may spend 1 MP per ally to give them advantage.","Regain {Power * points / 4} MP.","-1 on checks made from Intuitive Magic abilities, and on problems, instead pay the full amount of MP.","1",B.w3,"epic_source_intuitive_magic",!0,"MP","{2 * Power * points}",B.a8,B.a8,null)
B.aC1=new A.dm("source_prepared_magic","Prepared Magic","The caster can only cast magic that they have prepared in advance. You require an implement to use this source. They have {2 * Power * points} Max MP and start every Story with Full MP. Whenever they gain points of features, they may pick an equal number of points of features to form their spellbook. After each encounter, the character may prepare uses of their Prepared Magic features, choosing features with the source and features in their spellbook and the amount of MP spent to Prepare the Spell. Each prepared spell uses the MP spent as the Source value. Prepared spells must spend at least 1 MP, and no more than {1+Power} MP. You may prepare as many uses of any features in your spellbook that you can pay for. You may prepare the same feature multiple times.","You may have up to a total of {points} prepared skill spells per story. For each preparation, pick a skill; you may change what you have prepared at the end of a situation. When you perform a skill check, you may use a prepared skill to gain advantage. Your prepared skill spells are objects you can give to your allies to use as well.","Regain {Power * points / 4} MP.","-1 on checks made from Prepared Magic abilities, and on problems, instead pay the full amount of MP.","MP Spent",B.w3,"epic_source_prepared_magic",!0,"MP","{2 * Power * points}",B.a8,B.a8,null)
B.k0=new A.q2(2,"resourceWithSelection")
B.aCC=new A.c1("Flow","During your turn, You may spend 1 Ki point to Ready, Run or Retreat after the ability.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCo=new A.c1("Flurry","During your turn, You may spend 1 Ki Point to make 1 Melee Attack targeting an enemy range 1. On success, deal {Power d6}. Choose the defense targeted when you pick this.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCs=new A.c1("Restore","During your turn, You may spend 1 Ki Point to gain {Half Level d12} Regeneration.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCT=new A.c1("Breath","Before you would make an Int, Wis, or Cha defense, you may pay 1 Ki to gain advantage on the roll.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCK=new A.c1("Meditative","After you fail a concentration, spend 1 ki point and succeed instead.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCM=new A.c1("Present","You fail with a ki attack, you may spend a ki point to reroll the attack.",B.a8,!1)
B.amg=s([B.aCC,B.aCo,B.aCs,B.aCT,B.aCK,B.aCM],t.AJ)
B.aBV=new A.dm("source_ki","Ki","The character gains their powers from controlling their body's energy called ki. For each point spent on this source, the character gains 2 ki points, regaining all at the end of every situation. A character can activate their features using 1 ki point using a source of {Half Power} and they may trigger one of their ki effects. For every 2 points spent on this source, gain 1 of the below options.","You may pay 2 ki to reroll a skill you are proficient in one time.","Start the next situation with {Half points} extra Ki.","When you trigger a Ki effect, you must succeed a Vit Defense or lose the ki point without gaining a benefit from the effect.","{Half Power}",B.k0,"epic_source_ki",!1,"Ki","{2 * points}",B.amg,B.a8,"{points / 2}")
B.aC9=new A.c1("Vice","Gain {Half Vitality * Suffering} shield.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCw=new A.c1("Vengeful","Deal {Half Level * Suffering} bonus damage on attacks against enemies who have damaged your allies.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCc=new A.c1("Noble","You may make a status check vs cha, on success, pull an enemy {Suffering} spaces. You may instead target an ally and force them to move the same distance as you would have pulled an enemy.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCx=new A.c1("Loving","Adjacent allies heal {3 * Suffering}. Or target one ally anywhere and heal {Suffering}.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCV=new A.c1("Against Enemies","You and your allies gain +1 to attacks against enemies adjacent to your specter. Choose when you take this.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCI=new A.c1("From Enemies","You and your allies gain +1 to defenses from attacks from enemies adjacent to your specter. Choose when you take this.",B.a8,!1)
B.ao8=s([B.aCV,B.aCI],t.AJ)
B.aCr=new A.c1("Haunting","Target a free space within {Suffering} and summon a specter of your regrets that lasts until you activate this again or die.\nSpecters block their space, use your defenses, and you take half damage dealt to your specter ignoring resistance but not shield.",B.ao8,!1)
B.ajw=s([B.aC9,B.aCw,B.aCc,B.aCx,B.aCr],t.AJ)
B.aCN=new A.c1("Conceal","After you sacrifice to aid a reroll, you have -1 to Conceal for the rest of the scene.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCB=new A.c1("Convince","After you sacrifice to aid a reroll, you have -1 to Convince for the rest of the scene.",B.a8,!1)
B.aoz=s([B.aCN,B.aCB],t.AJ)
B.aC7=new A.dm("source_vice","Sacrifice","The character gains their power through self destruction, like drinking or stamp collecting. When you activate a power, you lose {Vitality + Level} health, and activate the ability with a source of {Power + 1}. You cannot reduce sacrifice damage by any means.\nEach time you sacrifice, gain 1 suffering to a max of {points}. Suffering is lost at the end of the situation.\nWhen you pick this the first time, pick a below option that triggers before or after you sacrifice.","Whenever you or an ally you can see gets problems on a skill, pay {Vitality + Level} health to allow them to reroll. For the rest of the scene, you have either -1 to Conceal or Convince. Choose when you first take this.","Reduce your sacrifice health cost by {Half Vitality}.","At the start of your turn, make a Wis defense, or you must trigger a sacrifice ability on your turn. If you end your turn without having done so, pay {Vitality + Level} health. If this kills you, all allies must pass a Wis defense or have -1 to all checks until the end of the scene from guilt.","{Power + 1}",B.k0,"epic_source_vice",!1,"Suffering","{points}",B.ajw,B.aoz,"{1}")
B.aCP=new A.c1("Sprint","During your turn, you may pay stamina to move extra spaces. You move up to 2 spaces further for each stamina spent. This doesn't alter your speed. Whenever you are under an effect that reduces your speed, you move 1 space per stamina instead.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCG=new A.c1("Dodge Roll","Before rolling a defense, you may spend {Vitality} stamina to gain advantage on the defense.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCF=new A.c1("Follow through","On success with an attack that deals damage, you may spend up to {Half Power} stamina to deal 1d6 extra damage per stamina spent.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCW=new A.c1("Leap","[Reaction] During your turn or at the end of an ally\u2019s turn, [Reaction] and Pay up to {Vitality} stamina, and dash to a free space within 2 * paid stamina.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCe=new A.c1("Stretch","Once per ability, you may pay 1 stamina to increase your range by 1.",B.a8,!1)
B.apd=s([B.aCP,B.aCG,B.aCF,B.aCW,B.aCe],t.AJ)
B.aBY=new A.dm("source_stamina","Stamina","The character gains their power through their physical endurance and strength. The character has {Power * points} Max Stamina, and regains all stamina at the end of the encounter. When they use a feature of this source, they may spend up to {Power} stamina, using the spent stamina as the source value. Breath: At the end of the round, if they haven't spent stamina this round, they gain {Power + Vitality} Stamina. For every 4 pts worth of combat features of the stamina source, gain 1 of the below abilities. You always know at least 1.","You may pay {half power} stamina to reroll a defense with a +1 to the result. You start the next encounter without this stamina.","During the next situation, whenever you Breath, regain {points / 3} extra stamina.","During the next situation, whenever you breathe, regain half the stamina.","{Power}",B.k0,"epic_source_stamina",!1,"Stamina","{Power * points}",B.apd,B.a8,"{points / 4}")
B.aC0=new A.dm("source_mutation","Mutation","You gain your powers from your body's ability to reorganize itself.\nYou have a Genepool of {points} combat features you select when you gain pts. You have {points} Evolution points at the start of every encounter. On your turn, You may spend evolution points to gain access to a feature in your genepool as a mutation. You may use the mutation for the remainder of the encounter with a source of {Half Power}. Mutations cost as many evolution points as they would feature points, and you may pay for upgrades up to the normal limit. You have a morph pool of {points / 3} Universal upgrades, and you may only use universal upgrades from your morph pool when you upgrade a mutation. When you trigger a mutation on later turns, you may pay for upgrades if possible. You may not exceed the normal feature upgrade limits. You must have a mutation to be able to use an ability in your genepool. You may pay twice the evolution cost of a mutation to give the mutation a source value of {Power} instead of {Half Power}.","{points / 3} times per Story, you may change your skill proficiencies or armor & fortitude values before making a check. This remains for the rest of the scene.","During the next situation: After activating a mutation ability, lose the mutation and regain those evolution points.","During the next situation, you reduce your max evolution points by 1.","{Half Power}",B.w5,"epic_source_mutation",!1,null,null,B.a8,B.a8,null)
B.NW=new A.q2(4,"time")
B.aBZ=new A.dm("source_time","Time","The character gains their power through altering time or predicting the future. After each encounter, you may select your chronomancy from 1 to {half points}. Your time source is {power - chronomancy}. At the start of a story, Roll and record {Chronomancy +1} attacks and {Chronomancy +1} skills you are proficient in. When you use this source you use one of your applicable chronomancy results, then roll a replacement result.\nYour chronomancy results don't benefit from +1 or -1 to success. Whenever you have advantage or disadvantage, select 1 result then roll the extra check. If you gain a reroll, reroll as normal. When you change your chronomancy at the end of a situation, you pick which results are lost, and you only make new rolls for gained chronomancy. You may use an Implement gaining any implement effects. If you do, you require that type of implement to use the feature.","When you make a skill check you have a recorded result for, you may use one of your applicable chronomancy results instead of rolling, then roll a replacement result.","Reroll half of your chronomancy results.","Set half of your chronomancy results to 1.","{power - chronomancy}",B.NW,"epic_source_time",!0,"Chronomancy",null,B.a8,B.a8,null)
B.aCg=new A.c1("Penetration","Pay 1 Psi Point and your ability ignores resistance.",B.a8,!1)
B.aD_=new A.c1("Drain","On Success, Pay up to {Half power} Additional Psi Points, to deal 1d6 extra damage and gain an equal amount of shield per Psi Point.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCj=new A.c1("Focus","Pay 1 Psi Point, and attacks ignore advantage, disadvantage, -1 and +1 to results for the attack and defenses caused by the attack.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCy=new A.c1("Distant","Pay 1 Psi Point and double the range of the ability or if the ability targets an area, increase the area size and range by 1.",B.a8,!1)
B.aCJ=new A.c1("Phasing","Pay 1 Psi Point, and your movement doesn't provoke attacks of opportunity and you ignore difficult terrain.",B.a8,!1)
B.apf=s([B.aCg,B.aD_,B.aCj,B.aCy,B.aCJ],t.AJ)
B.aC8=new A.dm("source_psionics","Psionics","The character uses their mind to alter reality. They have {2 * Power * points} Max Psi Points, regaining half after each encounter. When using a feature, They must spend at least 1 Psi Point and may spend up to {Power} Psi Points as the Source Value, and they may trigger one of their psi powers. They pick {points / 4} psi powers. You may use an Implement gaining any implement effects. If you do, you require that type of implement to use the feature.","You may spend 2 Psi Points to gain advantage on a skill you are proficient in or an Int, Wis, or Cha defense check. If an ally you can see is making a skill check that you have proficiency in, you may spend 2 Psi Points and that character rolls using your skill rather than their own.","Regain {Power} Psi Points.","-1 on checks made from Psionic abilities, and to trigger any of your Psi Powers you must make and succeed on a Defense vs Int first.","Psi Points Spent",B.k0,"epic_source_psionics",!0,"Psi Points","{2 * Power * points}",B.apf,B.a8,"{points / 4}")
